WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:16.641
Katie loved her star crown.

2
00:00:16.642 --> 00:00:21.504
She couldn't wait to wear it in Willow Creek's big birthday parade.

3
00:00:21.505 --> 00:00:26.126
But now she wanted day two of day camp to be finished.

4
00:00:26.127 --> 00:00:28.849
The Earthworms had work to do!

5
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.223
Finally it was eleven o'clock.

6
00:00:31.224 --> 00:00:34.525
Mrs. Penkov blew her whistle.

7
00:00:34.526 --> 00:00:38.494
"That's all for today, kids!" the camp leader said.

8
00:00:38.495 --> 00:00:41.968
"Please leave your hats and crowns on the shelf!"

9
00:00:41.969 --> 00:00:46.701
"Let's go, team," Katie said and headed for the door.

10
00:00:46.702 --> 00:00:51.829
Soon the Earthworms stood on the sidewalk outside the community center.

11
00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:55.100
Katie pulled open their shopping bag.

12
00:00:55.101 --> 00:00:57.519
"Look inside," she said.

13
00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.913
The Earthworms looked.

14
00:00:59.914 --> 00:01:03.472
"I don't see anything," said AJ.

15
00:01:03.473 --> 00:01:07.357
"Exactly," said Katie. "It's empty.

16
00:01:07.358 --> 00:01:10.210
The Earthworms are not doing well."

17
00:01:10.211 --> 00:01:12.952
Emily looked at the scavenger hunt list.

18
00:01:12.953 --> 00:01:16.250
"We need a menu," she said.

19
00:01:16.251 --> 00:01:18.711
"That's easy," said Luke.

20
00:01:18.712 --> 00:01:21.892
They headed for Fried Pie Heaven.

21
00:01:21.893 --> 00:01:25.955
"Sure, you can have a menu," said Aunt Sally.

22
00:01:25.956 --> 00:01:29.898
"But you're not the first team to come hunting here.

23
00:01:29.899 --> 00:01:31.835
Don't ask me who came though.

24
00:01:31.836 --> 00:01:35.535
I won't tell!" Aunt Sally laughed.

25
00:01:35.536 --> 00:01:38.524
The Earthworms frowned.

26
00:01:38.525 --> 00:01:41.642
Next they went to the post office.

27
00:01:41.643 --> 00:01:46.127
"Let me guess," said Pete, the post office clerk.

28
00:01:46.128 --> 00:01:48.761
"Not stamps. Not a postcard.

29
00:01:48.762 --> 00:01:52.069
You want a change-of-address form."

30
00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:55.231
"How did you know?" asked Emily.

31
00:01:55.232 --> 00:02:00.057
"Some scavengers came by yesterday," said Pete.

32
00:02:00.058 --> 00:02:03.253
"Rats!" said AJ.

33
00:02:03.254 --> 00:02:06.459
The Earthworms ran to the library.

34
00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:11.368
"We can get a calendar of community events here," said Katie.

35
00:02:11.369 --> 00:02:15.693
"Oh, look!" said Debra Donovan when they came through the door.

36
00:02:15.694 --> 00:02:18.624
"More scavengers!"

37
00:02:18.625 --> 00:02:21.280
The Earthworms groaned.

38
00:02:21.281 --> 00:02:26.584
The team left the library and walked slowly back down Main Street.

39
00:02:26.585 --> 00:02:29.619
They had three things in their bag.

40
00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:34.243
But it seemed like all the other teams were beating them.

41
00:02:34.244 --> 00:02:39.874
They crossed Walnut Street and came to Henderson's Gas Station and Auto Shop.

42
00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:42.299
Emily looked at the list.

43
00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:48.067
"Maybe Mr. Henderson has a pen with his business name printed on it," she said.

44
00:02:48.068 --> 00:02:51.595
"Anybody there?" Luke called.

45
00:02:51.596 --> 00:02:57.723
"I'm back here!" answered Mr. Henderson. "Come on in!"

46
00:02:57.724 --> 00:03:03.588
"Wow!" said AJ. "Look at that old car!"

47
00:03:03.589 --> 00:03:08.988
"This is a Model T Ford," said Mr. Henderson proudly.

48
00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:11.772
"The car that put America on wheels!

49
00:03:11.773 --> 00:03:14.207
And this is my grandpa."

50
00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:19.093
A very old man was wiping one of the car doors.

51
00:03:19.094 --> 00:03:23.021
"Grandpa Henderson found this car in an old barn.

52
00:03:23.022 --> 00:03:27.299
We've been working for two years to make it look like new."

53
00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.197
"Cool," said Emily.

54
00:03:30.198 --> 00:03:33.537
"Excellent!" said Luke.

55
00:03:33.538 --> 00:03:37.460
"But it's not on our list," thought Katie.

56
00:03:37.461 --> 00:03:43.486
"We're getting it ready for Willow Creek's birthday parade," said Mr. Henderson.

57
00:03:43.487 --> 00:03:48.275
"We're going to be in the parade too!" said AJ.

58
00:03:48.276 --> 00:03:54.412
"We think this was the first automobile in Willow Creek," said Grandpa Henderson.

59
00:03:54.413 --> 00:03:57.294
"It was made in 1920.

60
00:03:57.295 --> 00:04:00.275
It's almost as old as I am!"

61
00:04:00.276 --> 00:04:03.619
"How old are you?" asked Luke.

62
00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.625
"I'm 92."

63
00:04:06.626 --> 00:04:11.954
"You must be the oldest person in Willow Creek!" said Katie.

64
00:04:11.955 --> 00:04:15.583
"No, I'm not," he said, laughing.

65
00:04:15.584 --> 00:04:17.390
"But you know who is?

66
00:04:17.391 --> 00:04:20.405
My sister, Cora Mae Henderson!

67
00:04:20.406 --> 00:04:24.923
She is 103 years old."

68
00:04:24.924 --> 00:04:28.126
"One hundred three!" cried Katie.

69
00:04:28.127 --> 00:04:31.087
"This could be our big chance!"

70
00:04:31.088 --> 00:04:37.003
The Earthworms told Mr. Henderson and his grandpa about the scavenger hunt.

71
00:04:37.004 --> 00:04:41.730
"Have any other scavengers been here?" asked Emily.

72
00:04:41.731 --> 00:04:45.128
"No," said Grandpa Henderson.

73
00:04:45.129 --> 00:04:50.137
"Great!" said Katie. "We have to meet your sister."

74
00:04:50.138 --> 00:04:55.046
"Well, that could be a problem," said the old man.

75
00:04:55.047 --> 00:04:57.960
"She never comes to town."

76
00:04:57.961 --> 00:05:01.666
"We can go visit her!" said Katie.

77
00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:06.371
"Hmm . . . She doesn't like a lot of visitors," he said.

78
00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.942
"But you could try."

79
00:05:08.943 --> 00:05:13.766
He pulled a notepad from his pocket and started drawing a map.

80
00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:23.199
"First, you go way out to the end of Old Church Road . . ."
